  "reason": "Evidence: The largest single improvement in this search came from switching the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 (config_002→config_036: 0.635→0.706 acc), confirming that RNA representation is the most impactful design choice. However, scgpt has never been tested, leaving open the question of whether a generative pretrained encoder could outperform the variational scvi encoder. Question: config_042 (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) is a clean single-variable comparison to our current best (config_036), isolating the RNA encoder effect while holding image encoder, aggregation, fusion, and profile setting constant. Why this is the best next experiment: The RNA encoder dimension showed the largest effect size in our history, so resolving whether scgpt matches or exceeds scvi_n200 is the highest-uncertainty, highest-impact question remaining. If scgpt is competitive, it opens a new promising direction; if scvi_n200 still wins, we confirm the best encoder and can confidently pivot to exploring image encoder or aggregation choices in subsequent experiments."
}

